 one is rejected). It takes precedence over `orgPluginSettings` for that server in chat, Cowork and Code sessions alike; with no `toolPolicy` the server is left unrestricted. An entry whose name matches no installed plugin server does nothing.\n\nDesktop versions that predate `policy-only` do not recognise it: they drop the entry (listed under Configuration parse errors in the diagnostics report) and apply `orgPluginSettings` to that server instead. If every entry in the list is `policy-only`, those versions cannot read `managedMcpServers` at all: they report a parse error for it and, until they are updated, leave MCP servers that users added themselves, or that a project\'s `.mcp.json` declares, out of Code sessions. While older versions are still in use, keep the same permissions in `orgPluginSettings` too, and do not deploy a list made only of `policy-only` entries until every desktop has updated.'),rR=E.shortDescription(S.msg({defaultMessage:"Static headers sent on every request \u2014 routing and tenant headers only. No credentials here; use the headers helper script for tokens and rotating values.",id:"McpHeadersHint2"})),iR=E.shortDescription(S.msg({defaultMessage:"How long the helper\u2019s headers are reused before it runs again, in seconds. Defaults to 300.",id:"HtyK0/oE2w"})),oR=E.shortDescription(S.msg({defaultMessage:"Seconds before the TTL expires at which the helper re-runs mid-session. Defaults to 60. Keep it larger than the helper\u2019s typical runtime.",id:"zq1cbZBApQ"})),Mh=E.subfield(I.z.string().min(1),{label:S.msg({defaultMessage:"Name",id:"HAlOn1ZsuY"}),isPrimaryKey:!0,placeholder:S.msg({defaultMessage:"github",id:"Zejj2Gw5fy"}),description:{short:E.shortDescription(S.msg({defaultMessage:"Unique name for this server. Shown to users and used to key tool policy and sign-in state.",id:"40I9DtVbWB"}))}});os.PLUGIN_MCP_TOOL_POLICY_CHANNEL_NOTE=`For a plugin server that Claude Code launches or connects to itself (a marketplace plugin's), the permissions travel on Claude Code's managed-settings channel: another Claude Code [managed-settings source](${yi.COWORK_3P_DOCS_BASE}/code#interaction-with-claude-code%E2%80%99s-own-managed-settings) on the device replaces them unless that source sets \`parentSettingsBehavior\` to \`"merge"\`. \`blocked\` on a server the app connects to itself holds either way.`;var gc=E.subfield(os.ToolPolicySchema.optional(),{label:os.TOOL_POLICY_LABEL,support:{values:{"ask-session":{availableInVersion:"1.21459.0"}}},optionValues:Nt.TOOL_POLICY_EDITOR_VALUES,placeholder:S.msg({defaultMessage:"toolName",id:"iFhBHMeCjp"}),description:{short:E.shortDescription(S.msg({defaultMessage:"Lock the approval state for specific tools. Unlisted tools stay user-controlled.",id:"bS7WElxrrh"}),{docsOnly:!1}),long:E.longDescription("Also governs the same server when an installed plugin provides it. A plugin's MCP server matches an entry by URL, else by name (case-insensitive; a plugin server that runs locally matches by name only), and then follows that entry's `toolPolicy` alone: `orgPluginSettings` is not consulted for it, even when the entry sets no `toolPolicy`. A built-in entry (one with `server`) is the exception: it applies to a plugin's server of the same name only when a `toolPolicy` is written on it, and then carries that `toolPolicy` and the built-in's rule that its send and other irreversible tools cannot be loosened below `ask`, but not the built-in's other default prompts. An `http`, `sse` or `stdio` entry is also a server the app itself connects to or launches. To set permissions for a server that only a plugin runs, without the app connecting to or launching anything, use an entry with `transport: \"policy-only\"`.\n\n"+os.PLUGIN_MCP_TOOL_POLICY_CHANNEL_NOTE)}}),Tb={server:I.z.never({error:"server is only valid on built-in entries, which must not set transport/url/command"}).optional()};function sR(e){let t=(n)=>I.z.never({error:`${e} must not set ${n}`}).optional();return{url:t("url"),c