with or without a port or path, a single name, or a GUID; `name:digits` also reads as a host name with a port) is sent as `https://<value>`; an identifier with a scheme of its own (`urn:\u2026`, or an organization-defined one such as `VENDOR:URI:\u2026`) is sent exactly as written. A trust whose only identifier is a bare name or GUID will not match, because those are sent as `https://<value>`: add an `https://\u2026` or `urn:\u2026` identifier to the trust and enter that one here. With any other identity provider, use an absolute URI without a fragment (RFC 8707 \u2014 the IdP rejects one as `invalid_target`). Changing it signs users in again.")}}),redirectPort:zb,redirectHost:Fb,additionalRedirectReferrerHosts:jh({availableInVersion:"1.20186.0"})}).refine(...Ub).refine((e)=>{var t;return e.bearerTokenType!=="access_token"||!!((t=e.scopes)===null||t===void 0?void 0:t.trim())},{message:"scopes is required when bearerTokenType is access_token",path:["scopes"]})});var _c=R(function(XR){Object.defineProperty(XR,"__esModule",{value:!0});XR.credentialHeaderEntry=YR;XR.firstCredentialHeader=JR;XR.credentialHeadersWarn=Nae;var Bh=pn(),Iae=/^(?:authorization|proxy-authorization|cookie|set-cookie|token|secret|password|api-key|x-api-key|x-auth-token|x-amz-security-token|x-goog-api-key|ocp-apim-subscription-key|x-subscription-token|private-token|x-functions-key|x-honeycomb-team)(?:-?v?\d+)?$|(?:^|-)(?:tokens?|secrets?|password|passwd|signature|credentials?|authorization|(?:api|secret|access|private|signing|auth|license|master|encryption|session|client)-?(?:keys?|secrets?))(?:-?v?\d+)?$|(?:token|apikey|secretkey|accesskey|privatekey|signingkey|licensekey|sessionkey|clientsecret|password|passwd|credentials?)(?:-?v?\d+)?$/,Cae=/[_.\s]+/g,Tae=/^\s*(?:bearer|basic|token|digest)\s+\S/i,$ae=/\beyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{10,}\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{10,}\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{10,}/,Rae=/\b(?:AKIA|ASIA)[A-Z0-9]{16}\b/,Dae=/\b(?:bearer|basic)\s+(?=[A-Za-z._~+/=-]*\d)[A-Za-z0-9._~+/=-]{16,}/i,Mae=/\b(?:sk-[A-Za-z0